<!-- Globalesim Content -->
<div class="content-section">

  {% set primary = provider.codes | findCode(provider.primaryCode) %}
  <div class="content-callout">
    <h2>Globalesim Status &bull; {{ buildMonthYear }}</h2>
    <p>
      We can no longer verify Globalesim or the <strong>{{ provider.primaryCode }}</strong> code. As of {{ buildMonthYear }}, globalesim.com is not reachable as a working eSIM store (it's returned either a domain-parking page or a server error on our repeated checks), which is a strong signal the business behind it has shut down, moved, or is having serious technical trouble. We're marking the code invalid until we see evidence the site is back.
      <span class="callout-meta">Last checked <time datetime="{{ (primary.lastTested or buildTime) | fmtISO }}">{{ (primary.lastTested or buildTime) | fmtDate("MMM d, yyyy") }}</time>.</span>
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>What We Previously Verified</h2>
  <p>
    Globalesim used to sell eSIM data plans across a claimed 150+ countries, with the code <strong>{{ provider.primaryCode }}</strong> giving {{ primary.discount | lower }}. We're leaving that history here for reference, but since we can't currently reach the checkout page to confirm anything, don't try to buy from them until an active site turns back up.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to Go Instead</h2>
  <div class="decision-grid">
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--good">
      <h3>Working alternatives right now</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/holafly/">Holafly</a> for unlimited-data plans with a live, working checkout</li>
        <li><a href="/ubigi/">Ubigi</a> for similarly broad country coverage</li>
        <li><a href="/airhub/">Airhub</a> if you're looking for the cheapest per-GB pricing</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    For eSIM device compatibility, see our <a href="/compatible-devices/">eSIM compatible devices</a> guide.
  </p>

  <h2>Globalesim FAQ</h2>
  <div class="content-faq">
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Is {{ provider.primaryCode }} still working</h3>
      <p>No. We can't confirm it because Globalesim's own site no longer loads as a working eSIM store, so we've marked the code invalid.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>What happened to Globalesim</h3>
      <p>Their domain is no longer reachable as a working eSIM storefront: it's shown a generic domain-parking page on some checks and a server error on others. Either way, it's not the site we previously verified. We'll update this page if that changes.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>What should I use instead</h3>
      <p>See the alternatives above. Holafly, Ubigi, and Airhub are all live and currently verified on this site.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context":"https://schema.org",
    "@type":"FAQPage",
    "mainEntity":[
      {
        "@type":"Question",
        "name":"Is the Globalesim promo code still working?",
        "acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Globalesim's own site no longer loads as a working eSIM store, so the code is marked invalid and unverifiable."}
      },
      {
        "@type":"Question",
        "name":"What happened to Globalesim?",
        "acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Their domain is no longer reachable as a working eSIM storefront: it has shown a generic domain-parking page on some checks and a server error on others, neither of which is the site that was previously verified."}
      },
      {
        "@type":"Question",
        "name":"What eSIM provider should I use instead of Globalesim?",
        "acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Holafly, Ubigi, and Airhub are all live, working alternatives currently verified on this site."}
      }
    ]
  }
  </script>
</div>
